From e1ac7b5989fb35a010705ee272b0a62fbf15e524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Filippo Falezza <filippo.falezza@outlook.it>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 17:03:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 45/69] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7250: Describe the CPUs as a single
 cluster

The topology parser looks for core0, core1, ... in each cluster, so the
cluster1 { core6 } and cluster2 { core7 } nodes read as empty clusters
("/cpus/cpu-map/cluster1: empty cluster") and the whole cpu-map is
discarded. SM7250 is a DynamIQ design with all eight cores sharing the L3,
so describe them as one cluster, as SM8250 does.

This patch was generated by an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5 in
Claude Code) during an interactive bring-up session on a Motorola Moto G
5G Plus (XT2075-3, "nairo"). It has not yet been reviewed line by line
by a human and needs that review before any submission.

Assisted-by: LLM dtschema
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi
index 6e6c50e1c..34cbcb24a 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7250.dtsi
@@ -250,15 +250,11 @@ core4 {
 				core5 {
 					cpu = <&cpu5>;
 				};
-			};
 
-			cluster1 {
 				core6 {
 					cpu = <&cpu6>;
 				};
-			};
 
-			cluster2 {
 				core7 {
 					cpu = <&cpu7>;
 				};
